===Etymology===
{{borrowing|de|Gestalt|t=shape, figure, form}}. The German term can also apply to a geometric or graphical shape, but that is not the case when this word is used in English.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ɡəˈʃtælt/|/ɡəˈʃtɑːlt/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ɡəˈʃtɑlt/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[collection]] of [[physical]], [[biological]], [[psychological]] or [[symbolic]] [[entities]] that creates a [[unified]] [[concept]], [[configuration]] or [[pattern]] which is [[greater]] than the [[sum]] of its [[part]]s (of a [[character]], [[personality]], or [[being]])
#: ''This biography is the first one to consider fully the writer's '''gestalt'''.''

